{"timestamp":"2026-05-28T13:25:20.629Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_F0vmButEUSEzAW11rEwwmlwe","output":"Chunk ID: a1370f\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 1265\nOutput:\n---\nname: game-ui-frontend\ndescription: Design UI surfaces for browser games. Use when the user asks for HUDs, menus, overlays, responsive layouts, or visual direction that must protect the playfield.\n---\n\n# Game UI Frontend\n\n## Overview\n\nUse this skill whenever the game needs a visible interface layer. The job is not to produce generic dashboard UI. The job is to produce a readable, thematic browser-game interface that supports the play experience.\n\nDefault assumption: build the game world in canvas or WebGL, and build text-heavy UI in DOM.\n\n## Frontend Standards\n\n1. Establish visual direction before coding.\n   - Genre and fantasy\n   - Material language\n   - Typography\n   - Palette\n   - Motion tone\n2. Use CSS variables for the UI theme.\n3. Build clear hierarchy.\n   - Critical combat or survival information first\n   - Secondary tools second\n   - Rarely used settings behind menus or drawers\n4. Protect the playfield first, especially in 3D.\n   - The initial screen should feel playable within a few seconds.\n   - Default to one primary persistent HUD cluster and at most one small secondary cluster.\n   - Keep the center of the playfield clear during normal play.\n   - Keep the lower-middle playfield mostly clear during normal play.\n   - Put lore, field notes, quest details, and long control lists behind drawers, toggles, or pause surfaces.\n   - Prefer contextual prompts and transient hints over permanent boxed panels.\n5. Keep overlays readable over motion.\n   - Use backing panels, edge treatment, contrast, and restrained blur where needed.\n6. Design for both desktop and mobile from the start.\n7. Design 3D UI around camera and input control boundaries.\n   - Pause or gate camera-control input when menus, dialogs, or pointer-driven UI are active.\n   - Keep pointer-lock, drag-to-look, and menu interaction states explicit.\n\n## 3D Starter Defaults\n\nFor exploration, traversal, or third-person starter scaffolds, prefer this UI budget:\n\n- one compact objective chip or status strip at the edge\n- one transient controls hint or interaction prompt\n- one optional collapsible secondary surface such as a journal, map, or quest log\n\nDo not open every informational surface on first load. The scene should be readable before the user opens any deeper UI.\n\nAs a default implementation constraint for 3D browser games:\n\n- no always-on full-width header plus multi-card body plus full-width footer layout\n- no large center-screen or lower-middle overlays during normal movement\n- no more than roughly 20-25% of the viewport covered by persistent HUD on desktop unless the user explicitly requests a denser layout\n- on mobile, collapse to a narrow stack or contextual chips before covering the playfield with larger panels\n\n## Prompting Rules\n\nWhen asking the model to design or implement game UI, include:\n\n- the game fantasy\n- the camera or viewpoint\n- the player verbs\n- the HUD layers\n- the camera or control mode when the game is 3D\n- the tone of motion\n- desktop and mobile expectations\n- playfield protection and disclosure strategy\n- explicit anti-patterns to avoid\n\nUse `../../references/frontend-prompts.md` for concrete prompt shapes.\n\n## Motion Rules\n\n- Prefer a few meaningful transitions over constant micro-animation.\n- Reserve strong motion for state change, reward, danger, and onboarding.\n- Respect reduced-motion settings for non-essential animation.\n- Keep 3D HUD motion from competing with camera motion.\n\n## What Good Looks Like\n\n- HUD elements are legible without flattening the scene.\n- Menus feel native to the game world, not like a SaaS admin panel.\n- Layout adapts cleanly across breakpoints.\n- Pointer, keyboard, and game-state feedback are obvious.\n- In 3D games, menu and HUD states do not fight camera control or pointer-lock.\n- In 3D games, the first playable view keeps most of the viewport available for movement, aiming, and spatial reading.\n- Persistent information density is low enough that screenshots still read as game scenes, not UI comps.\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n- Generic app dashboard layouts\n- Flat placeholder styling with no theme\n- Default font stacks without intent\n- Dense overlays that obscure the playfield\n- Large title cards or multi-paragraph notes sitting over a live playable scene\n- Equal-weight boxed panels distributed around every edge of the viewport\n- Controls, objectives, notes, and lore all expanded at once on first load\n- Full-width top-and-bottom chrome with large always-on center or body panels in 3D play\n- Excessive motion on every element\n- Canvas-only UI when DOM would be clearer and cheaper\n- Forcing HUD controls into the 3D scene when standard DOM would be clearer\n- Letting camera input remain active under modals or inventory panels\n\n## References\n\n- Shared architecture: `../web-game-foundations/SKILL.md`\n- Prompt recipes: `../../references/frontend-prompts.md`\n- Low-chrome 3D layout patterns: `../../references/three-hud-layout-patterns.md`\n- React-hosted 3D UI context: `../react-three-fiber-game/SKILL.md`\n- Playtest review: `../../references/playtest-checklist.md`\n"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-28T13:25:20.629Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_IDW6owgpHBAbthYN9s4bVaEu","output":"Chunk ID: 197aeb\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 234\nOutput:\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n  <title>GameGmeta World Map</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"./styles.css\">\n</head>\n<body class=\"world-page\">\n  <main class=\"world-page-shell\" aria-label=\"GameGmeta world map\">\n    <header class=\"world-map-topbar\">\n      <div>\n        <strong>世界地图</strong>\n        <span id=\"worldMapMeta\">按保存时间排列地图方块</span>\n      </div>\n      <button type=\"button\" id=\"backToEditor\">返回地图编辑器</button>\n    </header>\n    <section class=\"world-map-stage\">\n      <div id=\"worldMapSurface\" class=\"world-map-surface standalone\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-label=\"World map grid\"></div>\n      <div id=\"worldMapTooltip\" class=\"world-map-tooltip\" hidden></div>\n    </section>\n  </main>\n  <script type=\"module\" src=\"./world.js?v=web-world-page-20260528\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-28T13:25:20.629Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_JnaDfEsKYN0R9EPkuBOLMsGX","output":"Chunk ID: 3afca0\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 1594\nOutput:\nconst SAVED_MAPS_STORAGE_KEY = \"gamegmeta_saved_editor_maps\";\nconst LEGACY_SAVED_MAPS_STORAGE_KEYS = [\"gamegmeta_saved_maps\"];\nconst PENDING_EDITOR_MAP_KEY = \"gamegmeta_pending_editor_map_id\";\n\nconst worldMapSurface = document.getElementById(\"worldMapSurface\");\nconst worldMapMeta = document.getElementById(\"worldMapMeta\");\nconst worldMapTooltip = document.getElementById(\"worldMapTooltip\");\nconst backToEditor = document.getElementById(\"backToEditor\");\n\nlet worldPlayerCell = null;\nlet worldLayoutState = null;\n\nfunction savedMaps() {\n  try {\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(SAVED_MAPS_STORAGE_KEY) || \"[]\");\n    if (Array.isArray(parsed) && parsed.length > 0) return parsed;\n    for (const key of LEGACY_SAVED_MAPS_STORAGE_KEYS) {\n      const legacy = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key) || \"[]\");\n      if (Array.isArray(legacy) && legacy.length > 0) return legacy;\n    }\n    return [];\n  } catch (_error) {\n    return [];\n  }\n}\n\nfunction chronologicalSavedMaps() {\n  return savedMaps().sort((a, b) => {\n    const left = String(a.createdAt || a.updatedAt || a.id || \"\");\n    const right = String(b.createdAt || b.updatedAt || b.id || \"\");\n    return left.localeCompare(right);\n  });\n}\n\nfunction worldLandLayout(mapCount) {\n  let cols = Math.max(24, Math.ceil(Math.sqrt(Math.max(1, mapCount) * 2.2)));\n  let rows = Math.max(16, Math.ceil(cols * 0.68));\n  let landCells = [];\n  while (landCells.length < mapCount) {\n    landCells = [];\n    const centerX = (cols - 1) / 2;\n    const centerY = (rows - 1) / 2;\n    const radiusX = Math.max(1, cols * 0.42);\n    const radiusY = Math.max(1, rows * 0.36);\n    for (let y = 0; y < rows; y += 1) {\n      for (let x = 0; x < cols; x += 1) {\n        const dx = (x - centerX) / radiusX;\n        const dy = (y - centerY) / radiusY;\n        const bulge = (\n          Math.sin((x + 1) * 1.7) * 0.13\n          + Math.cos((y + 2) * 1.3) * 0.10\n          + Math.sin((x + y) * 0.9) * 0.08\n        );\n        if ((dx * dx + dy * dy) < 1.0 + bulge) landCells.push({ x, y });\n      }\n    }\n    if (landCells.length < mapCount) {\n      cols += 2;\n      rows += 1;\n    }\n  }\n  return { cols, rows, landCells };\n}\n\nfunction worldCellKey(x, y) {\n  return `${x},${y}`;\n}\n\nfunction showWorldTooltip(event, text) {\n  worldMapTooltip.textContent = text;\n  worldMapTooltip.hidden = false;\n  const stageRect = worldMapSurface.getBoundingClientRect();\n  worldMapTooltip.style.left = `${event.clientX - stageRect.left + 14}px`;\n  worldMapTooltip.style.top = `${event.clientY - stageRect.top + 14}px`;\n}\n\nfunction hideWorldTooltip() {\n  worldMapTooltip.hidden = true;\n}\n\nfunction renderWorldPlayer() {\n  worldMapSurface.querySelector(\".world-player\")?.remove();\n  if (!worldLayoutState || !worldPlayerCell) return;\n  const player = document.createElement(\"div\");\n  player.className = \"world-player\";\n  player.style.left = `${(worldPlayerCell.x + 0.5) * 100 / worldLayoutState.cols}%`;\n  player.style.top = `${(worldPlayerCell.y + 0.5) * 100 / worldLayoutState.rows}%`;\n  worldMapSurface.appendChild(player);\n}\n\nfunction moveWorldPlayer(dx, dy) {\n  if (!worldLayoutState || !worldPlayerCell) return;\n  const next = { x: worldPlayerCell.x + dx, y: worldPlayerCell.y + dy };\n  if (!worldLayoutState.landKeys.has(worldCellKey(next.x, next.y))) return;\n  worldPlayerCell = next;\n  renderWorldPlayer();\n}\n\nfunction returnToEditor(mapId = \"\") {\n  if (mapId) {\n    try {\n      localStorage.setItem(PENDING_EDITOR_MAP_KEY, mapId);\n    } catch (_error) {\n      // Best effort only; editor still opens normally if localStorage is blocked.\n    }\n  }\n  window.location.href = `./index.html?build=from-world-${Date.now()}`;\n}\n\nfunction renderWebWorldMap() {\n  const records = chronologicalSavedMaps().filter((record) => record?.data);\n  const sourceRecords = records.length > 0\n    ? records\n    : [{ id: \"\", name: \"当前编辑器地图\", data: null }];\n  const layout = worldLandLayout(sourceRecords.length);\n  const landKeys = new Set(layout.landCells.map((cell) => worldCellKey(cell.x, cell.y)));\n  worldLayoutState = { cols: layout.cols, rows: layout.rows, landKeys };\n  worldPlayerCell = layout.landCells[0] || { x: 0, y: 0 };\n\n  worldMapSurface.innerHTML = \"\";\n  worldMapSurface.style.setProperty(\"--world-cols\", layout.cols);\n  worldMapSurface.style.setProperty(\"--world-rows\", layout.rows);\n\n  for (let y = 0; y < layout.rows; y += 1) {\n    for (let x = 0; x < layout.cols; x += 1) {\n      const cell = document.createElement(\"span\");\n      cell.className = `world-cell${landKeys.has(worldCellKey(x, y)) ? \" land\" : \" ocean\"}`;\n      cell.style.left = `${x * 100 / layout.cols}%`;\n      cell.style.top = `${y * 100 / layout.rows}%`;\n      cell.style.width = `${100 / layout.cols}%`;\n      cell.style.height = `${100 / layout.rows}%`;\n      worldMapSurface.appendChild(cell);\n    }\n  }\n\n  sourceRecords.forEach((record, index) => {\n    const cell = layout.landCells[index];\n    if (!cell) return;\n    const marker = document.createElement(\"button\");\n    marker.type = \"button\";\n    marker.className = \"world-map-marker\";\n    marker.style.left = `${(cell.x + 0.5) * 100 / layout.cols}%`;\n    marker.style.top = `${(cell.y + 0.5) * 100 / layout.rows}%`;\n    const name = record.name || `Map ${index + 1}`;\n    const label = `坐标 ${cell.x}, ${cell.y} / #${index + 1} / ${name}`;\n    marker.title = label;\n    marker.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", label);\n    marker.addEventListener(\"mouseenter\", (event) => showWorldTooltip(event, label));\n    marker.addEventListener(\"mousemove\", (event) => showWorldTooltip(event, label));\n    marker.addEventListener(\"mouseleave\", hideWorldTooltip);\n    marker.addEventListener(\"click\", () => returnToEditor(record.id || \"\"));\n    worldMapSurface.appendChild(marker);\n  });\n\n  renderWorldPlayer();\n  worldMapMeta.textContent = `${sourceRecords.length} 张地图；方向键/WASD 在绿色大陆像素块上移动，海洋不可进入。`;\n  worldMapSurface.focus();\n}\n\nbackToEditor.addEventListener(\"click\", () => returnToEditor());\nworldMapSurface.addEventListener(\"keydown\", (event) => {\n  const moves = {\n    ArrowUp: [0, -1],\n    ArrowDown: [0, 1],\n    ArrowLeft: [-1, 0],\n    ArrowRight: [1, 0],\n    w: [0, -1],\n    s: [0, 1],\n    a: [-1, 0],\n    d: [1, 0],\n  };\n  const move = moves[event.key];\n  if (!move) return;\n  event.preventDefault();\n  moveWorldPlayer(move[0], move[1]);\n});\n\nrenderWebWorldMap();\n"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-28T13:25:20.629Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_5Hc5Np9rQURKg7973YNvG16Z","output":"Chunk ID: 053f62\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 1011\nOutput:\n  background: #2c352f;\n}\n\n.asset-card img {\n  width: var(--asset-thumb);\n  height: var(--asset-thumb);\n  max-width: var(--asset-thumb);\n  max-height: var(--asset-thumb);\n  object-fit: contain;\n  object-position: center;\n  image-rendering: pixelated;\n  display: block;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n  background: #2a343b;\n}\n\n.asset-card span {\n  position: absolute;\n  width: 1px;\n  height: 1px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);\n}\n\n.asset-card small {\n  display: none;\n}\n\n.asset-card.asset-note {\n  aspect-ratio: auto;\n  width: 118px;\n  min-height: 68px;\n  padding: 10px;\n  place-items: start;\n  text-align: left;\n}\n\n.asset-card.asset-note span {\n  position: static;\n  width: auto;\n  height: auto;\n  overflow: visible;\n  clip: auto;\n  display: block;\n  color: #d9e5d9;\n  font-size: 12px;\n}\n\n.world-map-overlay {\n  position: fixed;\n  inset: 0;\n  z-index: 30;\n  display: grid;\n  place-items: center;\n  padding: 18px;\n  background: rgba(7, 12, 15, .82);\n}\n\n.world-map-overlay[hidden] {\n  display: none;\n}\n\n.world-page-shell {\n  width: 100vw;\n  height: 100vh;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-rows: auto 1fr;\n  background: #0a1216;\n}\n\n.world-map-panel {\n  width: min(1120px, 96vw);\n  height: min(820px, 92vh);\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-rows: auto 1fr;\n  border: 1px solid #536875;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  background: #111a1f;\n  box-shadow: 0 28px 80px rgba(0, 0, 0, .5);\n  overflow: hidden;\n}\n\n.world-map-topbar {\n  min-height: 64px;\n  padding: 12px 14px;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  gap: 16px;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);\n  background: rgba(20, 30, 35, .96);\n}\n\n.world-map-topbar strong {\n  display: block;\n  font-size: 18px;\n}\n\n.world-map-topbar span {\n  display: block;\n  margin-top: 5px;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  font-size: 12px;\n}\n\n.world-map-stage {\n  min-height: 0;\n  position: relative;\n  display: grid;\n  place-items: center;\n  padding: 18px;\n  background: #0a1216;\n}\n\n.world-map-surface {\n  --world-cols: 24;\n  --world-rows: 16;\n  position: relative;\n  width: min(100%, calc((100vh - 140px) * 1.5));\n  max-height: 100%;\n  aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;\n  border: 6px solid #092f42;\n  outline: none;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  image-rendering: pixelated;\n  background:\n    linear-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, .34) 1px, transparent 1px),\n    linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, .34) 1px, transparent 1px),\n    url(\"../assets/game/maps/world_pixel_blocks_20260528.png\") center / 100% 100% no-repeat,\n    #2c82bd;\n  background-size:\n    calc(100% / var(--world-cols)) calc(100% / var(--world-rows)),\n    calc(100% / var(--world-cols)) calc(100% / var(--world-rows)),\n    100% 100%,\n    auto;\n  box-shadow: 0 20px 64px rgba(0, 0, 0, .42);\n}\n\n.world-cell {\n  position: absolute;\n  display: block;\n  pointer-events: none;\n}\n\n.world-cell.ocean {\n  background: rgba(31, 125, 184, .36);\n}\n\n.world-cell.land {\n  background: rgba(99, 181, 76, .20);\n}\n\n.world-map-marker {\n  position: absolute;\n  z-index: 4;\n  width: 28px;\n  height: 28px;\n  min-width: 0;\n  min-height: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);\n  border: 3px solid #224e24;\n  border-radius: 0;\n  background: rgba(119, 209, 86, .92);\n  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 3px rgba(255, 255, 255, .16);\n}\n\n.world-map-marker:hover,\n.world-map-marker:focus {\n  border-color: #ffe76b;\n  background: #9deb6a;\n}\n\n.world-player {\n  position: absolute;\n  z-index: 5;\n  width: 26px;\n  height: 26px;\n  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);\n  background:\n    linear-gradient(#1b1b22 0 0) 50% 16% / 44% 24% no-repeat,\n    linear-gradient(#e8bb77 0 0) 50% 42% / 56% 34% no-repeat,\n    linear-gradient(#2b637b 0 0) 50% 78% / 64% 34% no-repeat;\n  image-rendering: pixelated;\n  filter: drop-shadow(0 2px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, .55));\n  pointer-events: none;\n}\n\n.world-map-tooltip {\n  position: absolute;\n  z-index: 7;\n  max-width: 260px;\n  padding: 8px 10px;\n  border: 1px solid #6f7e72;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  background: rgba(12, 19, 22, .94);\n  color: #f2f8ef;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  font-weight: 760;\n  pointer-events: none;\n  white-space: nowrap;\n"}}
